CORE
main.c
--unwindset f.0:1 -- --apply-loop-contracts _ --no-standard-checks
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
--
The reproducer of #9217. The do-while(0) loop of f is unwound once by a first
goto-instrument run, then loop contracts are applied by a second one. The loop
of acquire has no assigns clause and calls spin, whose loop has a contract.
Inferring the assigns clause of the loop of acquire must use a may-alias
analysis that is computed after the inlined loop of spin was instrumented; with
a stale analysis the instrumentation aborted with a CHECK_RETURN failure in
local_may_aliast::get.
